[E0437] Error: cannot yield a `str` that borrows `owned`
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:12:15 ]
    │
 11 │         val owned = String::of("a,b")
    │             ──┬──
    │               ╰──── `owned` declared here
 12 │         yield owned.toStr()
    │               ──────┬──────
    │                     ╰──────── `owned` is the generator's own, and moves with it
    │
    │ Help: yield a `String`, which owns its bytes, or make the value outside the generator, which then borrows it
    │
    │ Note: what a generator yields may borrow what it was given, but not what it holds itself, which moves with it
────╯
[E0439] Error: this loop's iterator borrows `owned` across a `yield`
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:19:22 ]
    │
 19 │         for piece in owned.split(",") {
    │                      ────────┬───────
    │                              ╰───────── each pass calls `next()` here, after the generator went on
 20 │             yield piece.len()
    │             ────────┬────────
    │                     ╰────────── the generator stops here
    │
    │ Help: make `owned` outside the generator, which then borrows it, or keep a copy that owns its bytes with `String::of(…)`
    │
    │ Note: a generator keeps its locals inside itself, and may be moved while it waits, so nothing may point into them across a `yield`; what lies on the heap, as a `Vec`'s elements do, stays where it is
────╯
[E0439] Error: `pair` is borrowed across a `yield`
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:29:13 ]
    │
 28 │         for y in pair {
    │                  ──┬─
    │                    ╰─── the loop walks it
 29 │             yield y
    │             ───┬───
    │                ╰───── the generator stops here, with `pair` borrowed
    │
    │ Help: walk `pair` by index, `for i in 0..pair.len() { yield pair[i] }`, or make it outside the generator, which then borrows it
    │
    │ Note: a generator keeps its locals inside itself, and may be moved while it waits, so nothing may point into them across a `yield`; what lies on the heap, as a `Vec`'s elements do, stays where it is
────╯
[E0439] Error: `hand` is borrowed across a `yield`
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:44:9 ]
    │
 43 │     for card in hand {
    │                 ──┬─
    │                   ╰─── the loop walks it
 44 │         yield card
    │         ─────┬────
    │              ╰────── the generator stops here, with `hand` borrowed
    │
    │ Help: take `hand` by reference, `&`, which the generator then borrows, or walk it by index, `for i in 0..hand.len() { yield hand[i] }`
    │
    │ Note: a generator keeps its locals inside itself, and may be moved while it waits, so nothing may point into them across a `yield`; what lies on the heap, as a `Vec`'s elements do, stays where it is
