[E0436] Error: `words` is used after `text`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:54:12 ]
    │
 52 │     var words = for w in text.split(" ") { yield w }
    │         ──┬──
    │           ╰──── `words` borrows `text`
 53 │     text.push(" c")
    │     ──┬─
    │       ╰─── `text` passed as `&var` here
 54 │     assert(words.next() == .Some("a"))
    │            ──┬──
    │              ╰──── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `words` before `text` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
[E0437] Error: `kept` would borrow a temporary
    ╭─[ err/200_generator_borrows/main.wip:56:16 ]
    │
 56 │     var kept = evens([1, 2, 3, 4])
    │                ─────────┬──┬──────
    │                         ╰─────────── an `Iterator<i64>` is kept here
    │                            │
    │                            ╰──────── a temporary, dropped at the end of the statement
    │
    │ Help: bind the value with `val` first, then borrow it
